# gate/ holds three different kinds of thing, and the tracked side of it is not
# one file — it is three: the gate's own reviewed material, plus the two ledgers
# a run writes (subject.json, deferred.json) and the one a human writes
# (overrides.json).
#
# TRACKED: the gate's own working material — the question it asks (prompts/) and
# the declaration of how it asks it (method.yaml). Those are reviewed.
#
# TRACKED, THOUGH A RUN OR A HUMAN WRITES THEM: subject.json and deferred.json,
# both run-written, and overrides.json, human-written — see the blocks further
# down this file for why each sits on this side of the line.
#
# IGNORED: every other thing a RUN produces — the resolved baseline, the release
# delta, the rendered site text, the per-surface captures, the run manifest,
# the wave bundle. Those are
# evidence for one release and are re-produced from scratch every time; a copy of
# one left in the tree is precisely the "found on disk" input the freshness check
# exists to refuse, and committing one would make it look authoritative.
#
# This is the pattern viewer-tests/.gitignore already uses for site-text.json,
# and it is written as "ignore everything, then name what is tracked" so that a
# per-run artifact added later is invisible by default. The landing script's
# stray check reads `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all`, which does
# not list ignored files but does list unignored ones and exits 2 rather than
# widening a write set — so an artifact that is not ignored here refuses the next
# lane's landing, whoever it belongs to.
*
!.gitignore
!method.yaml
!prompts/
!prompts/*.md
# subject.json is TRACKED, and it is the one per-run-written file that is. It
# records what this release froze its question to — the digest of surfaces.yaml
# at the first fan-out — so that a later round cannot widen the manifest without
# saying so. A freeze a run could regenerate is not a freeze, and a freeze git
# cannot see is one no human reviews; both are why it sits on this side of the
# line while every other artifact a run produces sits on the other.
!subject.json
# overrides.json is TRACKED for subject.json's reason, and one of its own: an
# override is a named human's ruling that a finding does not block this release,
# and a ruling nobody can see in a diff is a waiver rather than a decision. The
# file is refused when it is malformed, when a ruling names no reason or nobody,
# when it names a finding this run did not raise, or when it was ruled for another
# release — so an abandoned record is a failing gate rather than a quiet one.
!overrides.json
# deferred.json is TRACKED for subject.json's reason, and one of its own: a
# deferral nobody can see in a diff is a drop rather than a deferral, not a
# decision recorded anywhere a later reader can check. It is also read, not
# just written — the NEXT release's round one takes it as input — so it has
# to survive past the run that wrote it, which nothing else ignored here does.
!deferred.json
